          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A locally constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is a sheaf of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by open subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\}
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} restrictions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A|_{U_i}
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaves
          %p
            More elegantly said: locally constant sheaves are the sections of
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+stack"} constant stack
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Core(FinSet)\in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            of finite set, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi const
                    %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_C : Op(X)^{op} \to Grpd
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+presheaf"} presheaf constant
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that sends everything to (the identity on)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+stack"} constant stack
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stackification"} stackification
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi const
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar const_C : Op(X)^{op} \to Grpd
          %p
            Write then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            regarded as a sheaf or trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            over itself, i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in sheaves and hence in stacks over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \to \bar const_C
          %p are represented by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an open cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\}
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                over each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                a choice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i \in C
                of object in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                over each double overlap
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i j} = U_i \cap U_j
                an morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i j} : F_i|_{U_{i j}} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} F_j|_{U_{i j}}
            %li
              %p
                such that on triple overlaps we have
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                                %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                                %mi k
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                                %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i k}|_{U_{i j k}}= g_{j k}|_{U_{i j k}}\circ g_{i j}|_{U_{i j k}}
          %p
            Such data clearly is the local data for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with typical fiber any of the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Δ
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta \dashv \Gamma) : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{\overset{\Delta}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}} \mathcal{S}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            over base
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %p
            Without further assumption on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            we have the following definition.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to *
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{E}
              is called
              %strong
                locally constant and split by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              if in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/U
              we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \times U \simeq (\Delta S) \times U
                    \\,,
            %p
              for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              An object which is locally constant and
              = succeed "-split" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %em some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is called
              = succeed "." do
                %strong locally constant
            %p
              A locally constant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              which is in addition an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta Aut(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+object"} Galois object
              \.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            there is another characterization of locally constant sheaves.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+categories"} cartesian closed categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\, C \to D
              that preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed functor
              if the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(B^A) \to (F(B))^{F(A)}
            %p
              (which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A) \times F(B^A) \simeq F(A \times B^A) \to F(B)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            From the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            we have that
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \,\colon\, \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{E}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"} cartesian closed functor
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
          %p In this case the above definition is equivalent to the following one.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} = Sh(C)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Set
                      %mo *
                      %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \,\colon\, core(Set^\kappa_*) \to core(Set^\kappa)
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
              for sets of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              less than some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %p
              A
              %strong
                locally constant
                = succeed "-bounded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(p)
              along a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to core(Set^\kappa)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} (2,1)-topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(C)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This says that locally constant sheaves are the sections of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+stack"} constant stack
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi κ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} core(Set^\kappa)
            %p Notice that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    core(Set \kappa) \simeq \coprod_i \mathbf{B}Aut(F_i)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              is over all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal"} cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}Aut(F_i)
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of the set
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i
            %p
              This means that on each connected component of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              a locally constant sheaf is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \rho
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
              to an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta Aut(F)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              induced by the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : \mathbf{B} Aut(F) \to Set
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(F)
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              Specifically for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : * \to \Delta \mathbf{B} Aut(F) \simeq \mathbf{B} \Delta Aut(F) \hookrightarrow \Delta core(set)
              the classifying morphism of a locally constant sheaf and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to *
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              on which it trivializes, we have a pasting diagram of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi Δ
                                %mi Aut
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi Aut
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %msup
                              %mi Set
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi core
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Set
                              %mi κ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U \times \Delta F
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    P \times_{\Delta Aut(F) (\Delta (F // Aut(F)))}
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\Delta(F // Aut(F))
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\Delta Set^\kappa
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\to&amp; * &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} \Delta Aut(F)
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    \\Delta core(Set^\kappa)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F//Aut(F)
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-colimit"} 2-colimit
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \mathbf{B}Aut(F) \to Grpd
          %h3#internal_to_toposes
            Internal to
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*\colon X\to B
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in X
            is
            %strong
              locally constant internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            if there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_i U_i \to 1
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times U_i\to U_i
            is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^*\colon B\to X
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X/U_i \;\colon\; C\mapsto C\times U_i
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} slice (infinity,1)-topos
          %p
            When applied to the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi Fun
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B=Fun(P,\infty Grpd)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructible+sheaves"} constructible sheaves
          %h2#applications Applications
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Locally constant sheaves are sheaves of sections of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
            %li
              %p
                When used as coefficient objects in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
                they are also called
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+systems"} local systems
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
                on the fibers of a local system give rise to the notion of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            %li
              %p
                This may be used to define
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group+%28of+an+infinity-stack%29"} homotopy groups of
                general objects in a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+a+topos"} fundamental group of a topos
            %li
              %p
                This is the content of
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
          %h2#pattern Pattern
          %p In sufficiently highly locally connected cases, we have:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+function"} locally constant function
                is a section of a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaf
            %li
              %p
                a
                %strong locally constant sheaf
                is a section of a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+stack"} constant stack
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+stack"} locally constant stack
                is a section of (… and so on…)
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} locally constant ∞-stack
                is a section of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant ∞-stack
          %p
            A locally constant sheaf /
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructible+sheaf"} constructible sheaf
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The definition of
            %em locally constant sheaf
            originates in the notion of
            %em covering projection
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA
              4, Exposé IX, 2.0 .
          %p Lecture notes are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
              , section 6 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
          %p
            The topos-theoretic definition is reproduced in the context of a discussion of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+topos"} Galois topos
            as definition 5.1.1 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
              ,
              %em On the representation theory of Galois and Atomic Topoi
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0208222"}> arXiv:0208222
              )
          %p and definition 2.2 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
              ,
              %em The fundamental progroupoid of a general topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.1771"}> arXiv:0706.1771
              )
          %p or as definition 1 in
          %ul#BarrDiaconescu
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radu+Diaconescu"} Radu Diaconescu
              %em On locally simply connected toposes and their fundamental groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1981__22_3_301_0"}> NUMDAM
              )
          %p Discussion of the notions of locally constant sheaves is at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              %em Locally constant sheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2010/11/locally_constant_sheaves.html"}> blog discussion
              )
